 ## Unsettled
 
-- **Root questions versus sub-questions inside notes.** Weighted inbound links measure reuse when one note answers a local sub-question raised inside another note — what Commonplace's reader-need labels (`grounds`, `mechanism`, `defined-in`, `evidenced-by` in [link vocabulary](../reference/link-vocabulary.md)) already express. Thinking also organizes directly around recurring **root questions** rather than a single claim. Without explicit query-centered notes as roots, a top-level note that answers a live question can look orphaned if no other claim cites it, while a tightly linked cluster can answer each other's sub-questions in a closed loop without serving any real inquiry. We have no established way to represent query-centered root notes or propagate value from them down through answering notes and the notes that answer their sub-questions.
+- **Root questions versus sub-questions inside notes.** Weighted inbound links measure reuse when one note answers a local sub-question raised inside another note. Commonplace's reader-need labels already express that relation: `grounds`, `mechanism`, `defined-in` and `evidenced-by` in [link vocabulary](../reference/link-vocabulary.md). Thinking also organizes directly around recurring **root questions** rather than a single claim. Without explicit query-centered notes as roots, a top-level note that answers a live question can look orphaned if no other claim cites it. Without such roots, the notes in a tightly linked cluster can also answer each other's sub-questions in a closed loop without serving any real inquiry. We have no established way to represent query-centered root notes or propagate value from them down through answering notes and the notes that answer their sub-questions.
 - **Asymmetric selection pressure under autonomous production.** Structural validation, source grounding, and critique gates check validity more strongly than anything checks learning value or reader update. Under the conjecture that [weakly discriminated qualities tend to be underselected](../theory/weakly-discriminated-qualities-tend-to-be-underselected.md), an autonomous authoring loop can enrich accepted notes more strongly for validity than for usefulness, and if production favors fluent local additions, clutter can accumulate.
 - **Cold-start selection at admission.** Inbound links and counterfactual system use only become observable after a note has been retained and used. Autonomous production needs a way to filter, quarantine, or trial new candidates before those downstream signals exist.
 - **Combining dimensions without Goodharting.** Even where several signals exist (reader update, reuse of answers to sub-questions, root-question coverage, counterfactual use, maintenance cost), we do not yet know how to weigh them or when a coarse triage check outperforms a composite score.
